('89d7ed98-9247-44ac-9893-1617b2990600','en','Quartet for the End of Time','{}','A representative chamber music by Olivier Messiaen, composed in 1941.','Quartet for the End of Time connects Olivier Messiaen, Paris, its quartet, instruments, and historical events. The description is original editorial prose.','published'),
('92884b43-1a09-446f-8ef3-23e147ed5803','zh-CN','《无主之锤》','{}','皮埃尔·布列兹的vocal chamber music代表作，创作于1955年。','《无主之锤》在本图集中连接皮埃尔·布列兹、巴黎、cycle、相关乐器与历史事件。详情文字为原创策展摘要。','published'),
('92884b43-1a09-446f-8ef3-23e147ed5803','en','Le marteau sans maître','{}','A representative vocal chamber music by Pierre Boulez, composed in 1955.','Le marteau sans maître connects Pierre Boulez, Paris, its cycle, instruments, and historical events. The description is original editorial prose.','published'),
('a6c0030b-daa6-494a-8738-42756f5f2c25','zh-CN','《大气层》','{}','焦尔焦·利盖蒂的orchestral music代表作，创作于1961年。','《大气层》在本图集中连接焦尔焦·利盖蒂、布达佩斯、cluster texture、相关乐器与历史事件。详情文字为原创策展摘要。','published'),
('a6c0030b-daa6-494a-8738-42756f5f2c25','en','Atmosphères','{}','A representative orchestral music by György Ligeti, composed in 1961.','Atmosphères connects György Ligeti, Budapest, its cluster texture, instruments, and historical events. The description is original editorial prose.','published'),
('32db5513-58de-4027-a7ab-c739360b7b4e','zh-CN','《离子化》','{}','埃德加·瓦雷兹的percussion music代表作，创作于1931年。','《离子化》在本图集中连接埃德加·瓦雷兹、巴黎、ensemble、相关乐器与历史事件。详情文字为原创策展摘要。','published'),
('32db5513-58de-4027-a7ab-c739360b7b4e','en','Ionisation','{}','A representative percussion music by Edgard Varèse, composed in 1931.','Ionisation connects Edgard Varèse, Paris, its ensemble, instruments, and historical events. The description is original editorial prose.','published'),
('75002cc9-de42-48f3-aeed-7d4a9f974765','zh-CN','《布兰诗歌》','{}','卡尔·奥尔夫的scenic cantata代表作，创作于1936年。','《布兰诗歌》在本图集中连接卡尔·奥尔夫、慕尼黑、cantata、相关乐器与历史事件。详情文字为原创策展摘要。','published'),
('75002cc9-de42-48f3-aeed-7d4a9f974765','en','Carmina Burana','{}','A representative scenic cantata by Carl Orff, composed in 1936.','Carmina Burana connects Carl Orff, Munich, its cantata, instruments, and historical events. The description is original editorial prose.','published')
